eclaration commands","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"5773"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]}],"Name":"CommandDeclaration","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"5773"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[]},{"$id":"6794","$type":"DslCommandDeclarationTree","HasInput":true,"Children":[{"$id":"6795","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"COMMAND","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"5773"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"COMMAND","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"COMMAND"},{"$id":"6796","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"UpdateOperationParameterSpecification","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.PICore_MS.MSModel.Commands.UpdateOperationParameterSpecification","InfoMap":{"$id":"6797","FullIdObj":{"$id":"6798","$type":"IdentificableObject","Guid":"7337d881-8ccd-40fe-bce8-438fd1c8d5b5","Name":"UpdateOperationParameterSpecification","FullInfo":"Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.PICore_MS.MSModel.Commands.UpdateOperationParameterSpecification","TypeResolved":"","_project":{"$ref":"12"},"_domain":{"$ref":"5776"}}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"6798"},"Children":[],"Name":"CommandName","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"5773"},"Documentation":{"$id":"6799","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"Updates a Parameter Specification of the given Work Master Operation.\r\nApart from Id, each input argument is respective to one property of a Parameter Specification.\r\nThe command only updates the properties of the Parameter Specification given as input for which you pass a value. If you pass no value for an argument (other than Id), the respective property of the Parameter Specification is unchanged by the command.\r\nChecks if the given Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10824.\r\nChecks if the Work Master Operation associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300.\r\nChecks if the Work Master associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10812. If it exists but it is locked, it throws the error 10813.\r\nChecks if the given ParameterTargetValue, ParameterToleranceLow, ParameterToleranceHigh, ParameterLimitLow, ParameterLimitHigh values are of the same type than the given ParameterType value, otherwise it throws the error code 10835.\r\nIf the given Process Definition is different from the Process Definition defined in the Parameter Specification, the command checks:\r\n- if the given ProcessDefinitionNId exists, otherwise it throws the error 11210;\r\n- if the given argument SetToUseCurrentRevisionOfProcessDefinition is set to true, the property ProcessDefinitionRevision of the Parameter Specification will be deleted; if not, the command controls that the given argument ProcessDefinitionRevision exists for the given ProcessDefinitionNId; otherwise it throws the error 10895.","FullInfo":"Updates a Parameter Specification of the given Work Master Operation.\r\nApart from Id, each input argument is respective to one property of a Parameter Specification.\r\nThe command only updates the properties of the Parameter Specification given as input for which you pass a value. If you pass no value for an argument (other than Id), the respective property of the Parameter Specification is unchanged by the command.\r\nChecks if the given Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10824.\r\nChecks if the Work Master Operation associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300.\r\nChecks if the Work Master associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10812. If it exists but it is locked, it throws the error 10813.\r\nChecks if the given ParameterTargetValue, ParameterToleranceLow, ParameterToleranceHigh, ParameterLimitLow, ParameterLimitHigh values are of the same type than the given ParameterType value, otherwise it throws the error code 10835.\r\nIf the given Process Definition is different from the Process Definition defined in the Parameter Specification, the command checks:\r\n- if the given ProcessDefinitionNId exists, otherwise it throws the error 11210;\r\n- if the given argument SetToUseCurrentRevisionOfProcessDefinition is set to true, the property ProcessDefinitionRevision of the Parameter Specification will be deleted; if not, the command controls that the given argument ProcessDefinitionRevision exists for the given ProcessDefinitionNId; otherwise it throws the error 10895.","InfoMap":{"$id":"6800","FullIdObj":{"$id":"6801","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"Updates a Parameter Specification of the given Work Master Operation.\r\nApart from Id, each input argument is respective to one property of a Parameter Specification.\r\nThe command only updates the properties of the Parameter Specification given as input for which you pass a value. If you pass no value for an argument (other than Id), the respective property of the Parameter Specification is unchanged by the command.\r\nChecks if the given Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10824.\r\nChecks if the Work Master Operation associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300.\r\nChecks if the Work Master associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10812. If it exists but it is locked, it throws the error 10813.\r\nChecks if the given ParameterTargetValue, ParameterToleranceLow, ParameterToleranceHigh, ParameterLimitLow, ParameterLimitHigh values are of the same type than the given ParameterType value, otherwise it throws the error code 10835.\r\nIf the given Process Definition is different from the Process Definition defined in the Parameter Specification, the command checks:\r\n- if the given ProcessDefinitionNId exists, otherwise it throws the error 11210;\r\n- if the given argument SetToUseCurrentRevisionOfProcessDefinition is set to true, the property ProcessDefinitionRevision of the Parameter Specification will be deleted; if not, the command controls that the given argument ProcessDefinitionRevision exists for the given ProcessDefinitionNId; otherwise it throws the error 10895.","FullInfo":"Updates a Parameter Specification of the given Work Master Operation.\r\nApart from Id, each input argument is respective to one property of a Parameter Specification.\r\nThe command only updates the properties of the Parameter Specification given as input for which you pass a value. If you pass no value for an argument (other than Id), the respective property of the Parameter Specification is unchanged by the command.\r\nChecks if the given Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10824.\r\nChecks if the Work Master Operation associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300.\r\nChecks if the Work Master associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10812. If it exists but it is locked, it throws the error 10813.\r\nChecks if the given ParameterTargetValue, ParameterToleranceLow, ParameterToleranceHigh, ParameterLimitLow, ParameterLimitHigh values are of the same type than the given ParameterType value, otherwise it throws the error code 10835.\r\nIf the given Process Definition is different from the Process Definition defined in the Parameter Specification, the command checks:\r\n- if the given ProcessDefinitionNId exists, otherwise it throws the error 11210;\r\n- if the given argument SetToUseCurrentRevisionOfProcessDefinition is set to true, the property ProcessDefinitionRevision of the Parameter Specification will be deleted; if not, the command controls that the given argument ProcessDefinitionRevision exists for the given ProcessDefinitionNId; otherwise it throws the error 10895.","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"6801"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Updates a Parameter Specification of the given Work Master Operation.\r\nApart from Id, each input argument is respective to one property of a Parameter Specification.\r\nThe command only updates the properties of the Parameter Specification given as input for which you pass a value. If you pass no value for an argument (other than Id), the respective property of the Parameter Specification is unchanged by the command.\r\nChecks if the given Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10824.\r\nChecks if the Work Master Operation associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300.\r\nChecks if the Work Master associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10812. If it exists but it is locked, it throws the error 10813.\r\nChecks if the given ParameterTargetValue, ParameterToleranceLow, ParameterToleranceHigh, ParameterLimitLow, ParameterLimitHigh values are of the same type than the given ParameterType value, otherwise it throws the error code 10835.\r\nIf the given Process Definition is different from the Process Definition defined in the Parameter Specification, the command checks:\r\n- if the given ProcessDefinitionNId exists, otherwise it throws the error 11210;\r\n- if the given argument SetToUseCurrentRevisionOfProcessDefinition is set to true, the property ProcessDefinitionRevision of the Parameter Specification will be deleted; if not, the command controls that the given argument ProcessDefinitionRevision exists for the given ProcessDefinitionNId; otherwise it throws the error 10895.","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Updates a Parameter Specification of the given Work Master Operation.\r\nApart from Id, each input argument is respective to one property of a Parameter Specification.\r\nThe command only updates the properties of the Parameter Specification given as input for which you pass a value. If you pass no value for an argument (other than Id), the respective property of the Parameter Specification is unchanged by the command.\r\nChecks if the given Id exists, otherwise it throws the error 10824.\r\nChecks if the Work Master Operation associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10300.\r\nChecks if the Work Master associated to the given Work Master Operation Parameter Specification exists, otherwise it throws the error 10812. If it exists but it is locked, it throws the error 10813.\r\nChecks if the given ParameterTargetValue, ParameterToleranceLow, ParameterToleranceHigh, ParameterLimitLow, ParameterLimitHigh values are of the same type than the given ParameterType value, otherwise it throws the error code 10835.\r\nIf the given Process Definition is different from the Process Definition defined in the Parameter Specification, the command checks:\r\n- if the given ProcessDefinitionNId exists, otherwise it throws the error 11210;\r\n- if the given argument SetToUseCurrentRevisionOfProcessDefinition is set to true, the property ProcessDefinitionRevision of the Parameter Specification will be deleted; if not, the command controls that the given argument ProcessDefinitionRevision exists for the given ProcessDefinitionNId; otherwise it throws the error 10895."},"SystemAnnotations":[{"$id":"6802","$type":"DslKeywordNode","Text":"Protected","Children":[],"Name":"Keyword","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"5773"},"SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Protected","Siemens.SimaticIT.DSL.Plugin.ILeafNode.Text":"Protected"}],"CustomAnnotations":[{"$id":"6803","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"@Guid(7337d881-8ccd-40fe-bce8-438fd1c8d5b5)","FullInfo":"@Guid(7337d881-8ccd-40fe-bce8-438fd1c8d5b5)","InfoMap":{"$id":"6804","FullIdObj":{"$id":"6805","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"@Guid(7337d881-8cc